module vtd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The District of Vermont's own periods, computed under the federal rules
// (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule"). The memorandum periods of L.R.
// 7(a)(3) apply "unless the judge extends the deadline". Rules that state
// no period or limit stay out: materials accompanying a complaint and
// summonses (L.R. 3, 4), electronic filing and sealing (L.R. 5, 5.2),
// corporate disclosure (L.R. 7.1), appearances and withdrawal (L.R. 11),
// amended filings (L.R. 15), the final pretrial conference (L.R. 16),
// class actions (L.R. 23), interrogatory and production formats (L.R. 33,
// 34), exhibits (L.R. 40), consolidation (L.R. 42), jury costs (L.R. 47),
// taxable costs (L.R. 54), default (L.R. 55), registry deposits (L.R. 67),
// magistrate judges (L.R. 72, 73), certified questions (L.R. 74), clerk's
// orders (L.R. 77), removal (L.R. 81) and the admission, security and
// conduct rules (L.R. 83.1-83.5). Periods the rules state in units
// lit/core does not count stay in notes: the original of a facsimile
// filing within 3 business days (L.R. 10(b)(3)) and objections and
// counter-designations to videotaped deposition designations within 7
// business days after service (L.R. 26(d)). Periods measured from the
// "later of" two dates stay in notes: the third-party discovery
// completion date, the later of the approved schedule's date or 3 months
// after the third-party answer or appearance (L.R. 26(b)(2)), and the
// response to an opposing party's additional facts, within fourteen days
// or when its response to a cross-motion is due, if later (L.R. 56(b)).
// The bankruptcy notice of appeal "within 14 calendar days" (L.R.
// 9(b)(1)) restates FRBP 8002(a)(1) and is lit/frbp's. Amounts are not
// declared: the $500 neutral evaluator's fee (L.R. 16.1(d)(3)) and the
// $.50 per page photocopy rate (L.R. 40(e)(2)). The L.R. 26(a)(4)(G) and
// (J) schedule items that L.R. 16.1(e)(1)(D) and 56(e) cite are not in the
// vendored L.R. 26(a)(4), which states only the form. The earlier D. Vt.
// outline's FRCP flow and its Supreme Court decisions (Twombly, Iqbal,
// Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby) are FRCP authority and belong to
// lit/frcp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A memorandum supporting or opposing a dispositive motion: at most 25
/// pages, excluding exhibits and attachments, unless the judge grants
/// prior leave (L.R. 7(a)(4)(A)).
limit dispositive-memorandum {
  pages <= 25 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 7(a)(4)(A)"
} cite "D. Vt. L.R. 7(a)(4)(A)"

/// A memorandum supporting or opposing a non-dispositive motion: at most
/// 15 pages, excluding exhibits and attachments (L.R. 7(a)(4)(B)).
limit nondispositive-memorandum {
  pages <= 15 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 7(a)(4)(B)"
} cite "D. Vt. L.R. 7(a)(4)(B)"

/// A reply memorandum: at most 10 pages, excluding exhibits and
/// attachments (L.R. 7(a)(5)(B)).
limit reply-memorandum { pages <= 10 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 7(a)(5)(B)" } cite "D. Vt. L.R. 7(a)(5)(B)"

/// Motions and memoranda in a Social Security case: a total of at most 25
/// pages (L.R. 9(a)(6)(A)).
limit social-security-memorandum {
  pages <= 25 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 9(a)(6)(A)"
} cite "D. Vt. L.R. 9(a)(6)(A)"

/// An early neutral evaluation statement: at most 10 pages, excluding
/// exhibits and attachments (L.R. 16.1(h)(1)(A)).
limit evaluation-statement {
  pages <= 10 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 16.1(h)(1)(A)"
} cite "D. Vt. L.R. 16.1(h)(1)(A)"

/// A dispositive motion, such as a motion to dismiss or for summary
/// judgment, is served (L.R. 7(a)(3)(A)).
event DispositiveMotionServed() paper dispositive-memorandum
/// Any other motion is served (L.R. 7(a)(3)(B)).
event MotionServed() paper nondispositive-memorandum
/// A memorandum opposing a motion is filed (L.R. 7(a)(5)).
event OppositionFiled()
/// A reply memorandum is filed (L.R. 7(a)(5)).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-memorandum
/// The court order sought to be reconsidered is entered (L.R. 7(c)).
event OrderEntered()
/// Notice of a Social Security action is given under Rule 3 (L.R.
/// 9(a)(1)).
event SocialSecurityNoticeGiven()
/// The Commissioner files an answer (L.R. 9(a)(2)).
event CommissionerAnswerFiled()
/// The plaintiff files the Motion for Order Reversing the Commissioner's
/// Decision (L.R. 9(a)(3)).
event ReversalMotionFiled() paper social-security-memorandum
/// The Commissioner files the Motion for Order Affirming the
/// Commissioner's Decision (L.R. 9(a)(4)).
event AffirmanceMotionFiled() paper social-security-memorandum
/// The plaintiff's reply raising new issues or arguments is served (L.R.
/// 9(a)(5)).
event SocialSecurityReplyServed()
/// The designation of the record on a bankruptcy appeal is filed (L.R.
/// 9(b)(2)).
event DesignationFiled()
/// A motion for withdrawal of reference is served (L.R. 9(d)(2)).
event WithdrawalMotionServed()
/// An opposition to withdrawal of reference is served (L.R. 9(d)(2)).
event WithdrawalOppositionServed()
/// The ENE Administrator mails the list of potential evaluators (L.R.
/// 16.1(e)(1)(B)).
event EvaluatorListMailed()
/// A party learns of an evaluator's possible conflict of interest (L.R.
/// 16.1(e)(2)).
event ConflictLearned()
/// The early neutral evaluation session is held (L.R. 16.1(g)-(k)).
event EneSessionHeld()
/// An early neutral evaluation statement is served (L.R. 16.1(h)(1)).
event EvaluationStatementServed() paper evaluation-statement
/// Any defendant is served with the complaint (L.R. 26(a)(2)).
event DefendantServed()
/// Any defendant appears (L.R. 26(a)(2)).
event DefendantAppeared()
/// The last answer is filed (L.R. 26(a)(1)).
event LastAnswerFiled()
/// The third-party answer is filed or the third party otherwise appears
/// (L.R. 26(b)(1)).
event ThirdPartyAppeared()
/// Trial or a hearing begins on the date scheduled (L.R. 26(d), 45(a),
/// 51(a), 52).
event TrialBegins()

/// L.R. 7(a)(3)(A): unless the judge extends the deadline, a memorandum
/// opposing a dispositive motion is filed no more than 30 days after the
/// motion is served.
deadline dispositive-opposition-period: 30.days after DispositiveMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 7(a)(3)(A)"
/// L.R. 7(a)(3)(B): unless the judge extends the deadline, a memorandum in
/// opposition to any other motion is filed no more than 14 days after the
/// motion is served.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 7(a)(3)(B)"
/// L.R. 7(a)(5)(A): a reply memorandum is filed no more than 14 days after
/// an opposing memorandum.
deadline reply-period: 14.days after OppositionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 7(a)(5)(A)"
/// L.R. 7(c): a motion to reconsider a court order, other than one
/// governed by FRCP 59 or 60, is filed within 14 days from the date of the
/// order.
deadline reconsideration-period: 14.days after OrderEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 7(c)"
/// L.R. 9(a)(1): within 60 days after notice of a Social Security action
/// is given under Rule 3, the Commissioner serves and files an answer.
deadline commissioner-answer-period: 60.days after SocialSecurityNoticeGiven() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 9(a)(1)"
/// L.R. 9(a)(2): within 30 days after the Commissioner files an answer,
/// the plaintiff serves and files a Motion for Order Reversing the
/// Commissioner's Decision and a supporting memorandum.
deadline reversal-motion-period: 30.days after CommissionerAnswerFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 9(a)(2)"
/// L.R. 9(a)(3): within 30 days after the plaintiff's motion, the
/// Commissioner serves and files a Motion for Order Affirming the Decision
/// of the Commissioner and a supporting memorandum.
deadline affirmance-motion-period: 30.days after ReversalMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 9(a)(3)"
/// L.R. 9(a)(4): within 14 days after the Commissioner's motion, the
/// plaintiff may serve and file a reply.
deadline social-security-reply-period: 14.days after AffirmanceMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 9(a)(4)"
/// L.R. 9(a)(5): if the reply raises new issues or arguments, the
/// Commissioner may serve and file a sur-reply within 14 days after
/// service of the reply.
deadline social-security-sur-reply-period: 14.days after SocialSecurityReplyServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 9(a)(5)"
/// L.R. 9(b)(2): the designating party complies with the bankruptcy court
/// clerk's requests to assemble and transmit the record to the district
/// court within 30 calendar days after filing the designation.
deadline record-transmission-period: 30.days after DesignationFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 9(b)(2)"
/// L.R. 9(d)(2): an opposition to withdrawal of reference is filed within
/// 14 calendar days after service of the motion.
deadline withdrawal-opposition-period: 14.days after WithdrawalMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 9(d)(2)"
/// L.R. 9(d)(2): the moving party has 14 calendar days after service of
/// the opposition to file a reply.
deadline withdrawal-reply-period: 14.days after WithdrawalOppositionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 9(d)(2)"
/// L.R. 16.1(e)(1)(B), (C): each party reports its evaluator selection, or
/// each side its strike, to the ENE Administrator in writing within 14
/// days from when the list is mailed.
deadline evaluator-selection-period: 14.days after EvaluatorListMailed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 16.1(e)(1)(B)"
/// L.R. 16.1(e)(2): a party who believes an evaluator has a conflict of
/// interest notifies the ENE Administrator within 7 days of learning of
/// it; otherwise the objection is waived.
deadline evaluator-conflict-period: 7.days after ConflictLearned() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 16.1(e)(2)"
/// L.R. 16.1(g)(3)(B): a written request to be excused from attending the
/// ENE session is filed at least 21 calendar days before the session date.
deadline ene-excusal-period: 21.days before EneSessionHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 16.1(g)(3)(B)"
/// L.R. 16.1(h)(1): at least 14 days before the ENE session, each party
/// submits to the evaluator and serves its written evaluation statement.
deadline evaluation-statement-period: 14.days before EneSessionHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 16.1(h)(1)"
/// L.R. 16.1(j)(1): within 21 calendar days after the ENE session, the
/// evaluator files and sends the evaluator's report.
deadline evaluator-report-period: 21.days after EneSessionHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 16.1(j)(1)"
/// L.R. 16.1(k)(1)(D): a supplemental evaluator's report is filed within
/// 60 days from the date of the session.
deadline supplemental-report-period: 60.days after EneSessionHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 16.1(k)(1)(D)"
/// L.R. 26(a)(1): the parties' Discovery Schedule provides for completion
/// of discovery no later than 8 months after the last answer was filed.
deadline discovery-completion-period: 8.months after LastAnswerFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 26(a)(1)"
/// L.R. 26(a)(2): the Discovery Schedule is filed within the earlier of 75
/// days after any defendant has been served with the complaint or 45 days
/// after any defendant has appeared (with `discovery-schedule-appearance-period`;
/// the earlier date controls). Otherwise the case is set for a scheduling
/// conference.
deadline discovery-schedule-service-period: 75.days after DefendantServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 26(a)(2)"
/// L.R. 26(a)(2): the Discovery Schedule is filed within the earlier of 75
/// days after service or 45 days after any defendant has appeared.
deadline discovery-schedule-appearance-period: 45.days after DefendantAppeared() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 26(a)(2)"
/// L.R. 26(b)(1): a third-party discovery schedule is filed no more than
/// 45 days after the third-party answer is filed or the third party has
/// otherwise appeared.
deadline third-party-schedule-period: 45.days after ThirdPartyAppeared() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 26(b)(1)"
/// L.R. 26(d): unless the court orders otherwise, at least 30 days before
/// trial counsel provide opposing counsel the designated portions of
/// videotaped depositions they intend to offer under FRCP 32(a)(6).
deadline video-designation-period: 30.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 26(d)"
/// L.R. 45(a): at least 30 days before the trial or hearing, a party
/// proceeding in forma pauperis or pro se who requires a witness by
/// subpoena or writ files a witness list and a statement of each
/// witness's expected testimony.
deadline subpoena-witness-list-period: 30.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 45(a)"
/// L.R. 51(a): requests for jury instructions are filed at least 14 days
/// before the scheduled trial date.
deadline jury-instructions-period: 14.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 51(a)"
/// L.R. 52: absent leave, when trial is by the court, the parties submit
/// proposed findings of fact and conclusions of law at least 14 days
/// before the scheduled trial date.
deadline proposed-findings-period: 14.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "D. Vt. L.R. 52"
